[{"text": "I now give the floor", "start": 2.36, "duration": 7.64}, {"text": "to His Excellency Nasser Bourita,", "start": 5.68, "duration": 6.92}, {"text": "Minister of Foreign Affairs, African", "start": 10.0, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "Cooperation, and Moroccans Abroad of", "start": 12.6, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Morocco.", "start": 15.64, "duration": 2.64}, {"text": ">> Mr. President of the General Assembly", "start": 36.52, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": ">> Your Excellency, President of the", "start": 38.88, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "General Assembly, Mr. Secretary-General,", "start": 41.28, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "Your Excellencies,", "start": 44.4, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 46.44, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "I extend my sincere congratulations uh", "start": 51.32, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "on behalf of the delegation of the", "start": 55.6, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Kingdom of Morocco to His Excellency", "start": 57.12, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "Mr. Khali Rahman on his election as", "start": 59.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "President of the General Assembly at its", "start": 62.36, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "81st session, and I wish him every", "start": 64.4, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "success in his lofty mission.", "start": 66.84, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "I also commend the tireless efforts of", "start": 69.24, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Secretary-General Antonio Guterres", "start": 72.16, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "since", "start": 74.92, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "he assumed the leadership of our", "start": 77.64, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "organization.", "start": 79.4, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "Amid the major divisions the world has", "start": 80.76, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "experienced over the past decade, he has", "start": 83.28, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "emerged as a voice of wisdom, consensus,", "start": 85.92, "duration": 7.32}, {"text": "and pragmatism, defending tirelessly and", "start": 89.32, "duration": 7.48}, {"text": "courageously the United Nations system", "start": 93.24, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "and international law", "start": 96.8, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "as the two fundamental pillars", "start": 99.08, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "for the maintenance of international", "start": 102.36, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "peace and security.", "start": 104.24, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "Mr. Guterres has remained a symbol of", "start": 107.04, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "multilateral diplomacy and of", "start": 109.72, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "international cooperation in overcoming", "start": 111.96, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "the turmoil and obstacles facing our", "start": 114.56, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "world today.", "start": 117.48, "duration": 2.76}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 120.6, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "the most apt description of our", "start": 122.64, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "international reality is the one", "start": 124.8, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "expressed by his majesty King Mohammed", "start": 126.8, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "VI,", "start": 130.64, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "may God assist him, when his majesty", "start": 131.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "said and I quote, \"The world is changing", "start": 135.0, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "at an unprecedented pace and certainties", "start": 137.16, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "are steadily receding. This has led to a", "start": 140.48, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "blurring of standards and concepts.", "start": 143.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Alliances have become open question.", "start": 145.64, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "International law is frequently", "start": 148.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "violated.\"", "start": 150.0, "duration": 2.92}, {"text": "And its capacity to regulate", "start": 153.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "international relations faces numerous", "start": 155.4, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "challenges.", "start": 158.2, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "End of quote from his majesty the king.", "start": 160.92, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "We are therefore facing a world whose", "start": 164.28, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "fundamental features are the following.", "start": 167.32, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "First, the escalation of acute and", "start": 170.12, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "diverse international crises,", "start": 172.32, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "military, economic, energy-related, and", "start": 174.8, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "environmental. Second,", "start": 178.16, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "the spread of confrontational tendencies", "start": 180.44, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "as a key determinant of relations", "start": 183.88, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "between states. Third,", "start": 186.0, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "the difficulty of predicting the outcome", "start": 188.68, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "of crises.", "start": 191.04, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "We know when they begin,", "start": 192.56, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "but not when they will end. Fourth,", "start": 194.72, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "the diminishing capacity of existing", "start": 198.239, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "regulatory structures to play the role", "start": 200.88, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "in preventing and managing crises.", "start": 203.6, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "In this complex international context,", "start": 206.64, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Mr. President, I wish to focus on three", "start": 209.48, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "areas", "start": 212.0, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "to which the international community", "start": 213.48, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "must accord priority. First, confronting", "start": 215.12, "duration": 6.839}, {"text": "non-state armed groups as a threat to", "start": 218.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "international security and stability.", "start": 221.959, "duration": 3.881}, {"text": "Second,", "start": 224.36, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "addressing climate change and its", "start": 225.84, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "effects. Third,", "start": 228.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "tackling regional challenges,", "start": 230.2, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "particularly in the Middle East and", "start": 232.32, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "Africa.", "start": 234.6, "duration": 2.56}, {"text": "The role of non-state armed groups", "start": 237.52, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "that threaten the security and stability", "start": 240.64, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "of states has grown considerably.", "start": 243.2, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "Indeed, they now seek to control", "start": 246.2, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "maritime corridors and straits and to", "start": 248.52, "duration": 6.439}, {"text": "threaten freedom of navigation.", "start": 252.0, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "They also target facilities in a number", "start": 254.959, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "of countries.", "start": 257.2, "duration": 4.039}, {"text": "At the global level, more than 200", "start": 258.48, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "million people live in areas under the", "start": 261.239, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "control of armed groups or in contested", "start": 263.56, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "areas.", "start": 267.16, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "Moreover, more than 130", "start": 268.56, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "non-state armed groups have been", "start": 272.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "identified as legally classified parties", "start": 274.44, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "to armed conflicts.", "start": 277.76, "duration": 3.159}, {"text": "These figures", "start": 279.4, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "clearly reflect", "start": 280.919, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "the scale of the spread and", "start": 282.76, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "proliferation of these groups in a world", "start": 285.16, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "that over the past two decades has", "start": 288.28, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "become less secure and less stable.", "start": 290.6, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "Further, the close links between these", "start": 295.16, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "armed groups and separatist militias", "start": 297.84, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "on the one hand and terrorist", "start": 302.12, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "organizations and criminal networks, as", "start": 304.84, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "well as mercenary elements on the other", "start": 307.52, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "hand, are evident to all. It is", "start": 309.56, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "therefore a mistake to believe that some", "start": 311.76, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "of these", "start": 313.76, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "groups are peaceful or constructive or", "start": 314.8, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "that they can engage in the settlement", "start": 317.919, "duration": 6.601}, {"text": "of conflicts. All these groups use", "start": 321.36, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "violence to impose a fait accompli and", "start": 324.52, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "to serve the agenda of those who control", "start": 327.16, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "them.", "start": 329.6, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "They must therefore be dealt with", "start": 331.48, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "firmly.", "start": 333.4, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "And responsibility must be assigned to", "start": 335.04, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "the states that sponsor, harbor,", "start": 337.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "finance, and arm them and provide them", "start": 339.72, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "with safe haven and support.", "start": 342.76, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "The responsibility of these sponsoring", "start": 345.88, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "states is not merely political. It is", "start": 347.8, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "also legal, moral,", "start": 350.24, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and historical.", "start": 352.8, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "These groups and their sponsors alike", "start": 355.28, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "cannot be allowed to become a means of", "start": 358.96, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "evading responsibility or a tool for", "start": 361.4, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "carrying out what states cannot do", "start": 364.4, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "directly.", "start": 367.24, "duration": 2.68}, {"text": "Hence,", "start": 370.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "deterrent sanctions must", "start": 372.24, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "be imposed on these groups and their", "start": 374.72, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "sponsors.", "start": 376.6, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "All those who provide them with support,", "start": 378.48, "duration": 3.439}, {"text": "financing, or arms must be held", "start": 380.32, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "accountable. Mr. President,", "start": 381.919, "duration": 5.561}, {"text": "there can be no way to sustain", "start": 384.96, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "peace and development without", "start": 387.48, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "effectively addressing the challenge of", "start": 389.88, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "climate change,", "start": 392.24, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "which is no longer a future threat.", "start": 394.32, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "It is already affecting water and food", "start": 397.96, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "security,", "start": 400.24, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "as well as the stability of territories,", "start": 402.32, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "economies, and the living conditions of", "start": 405.16, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "populations.", "start": 407.52, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Despite its limited contribution to", "start": 409.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "greenhouse gas emissions, Morocco", "start": 411.76, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "remains among the countries most", "start": 415.08, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "vulnerable to the impacts of climate", "start": 417.24, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "change. Accordingly,", "start": 419.32, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "in line with the vision of His Majesty", "start": 421.48, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "King Mohammed the VI, may God assist", "start": 423.96, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "him, the kingdom has adopted a proactive", "start": 426.919, "duration": 5.321}, {"text": "policy based on the continued", "start": 429.72, "duration": 3.96}, {"text": "construction of dams, the", "start": 432.24, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "interconnection of water basins,", "start": 433.68, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "seawater desalination,", "start": 435.84, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "the reuse of treated wastewater, and the", "start": 438.28, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "rationalization of water resource", "start": 440.64, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "management, particularly in the", "start": 442.4, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "agricultural sector.", "start": 443.96, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "This national effort forms part of an", "start": 446.0, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "international commitment to climate", "start": 448.52, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "action. On that basis, the kingdom has", "start": 450.16, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "set for the period of 2026-2035", "start": 452.72, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "a target of reducing greenhouse gas", "start": 456.8, "duration": 7.72}, {"text": "emissions by up to 53%", "start": 460.56, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "by 2035", "start": 464.52, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "while placing adaptation and", "start": 466.68, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "strengthening of territorial", "start": 469.32, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "resilience", "start": 471.64, "duration": 3.96}, {"text": "at the top of its priorities.", "start": 473.16, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "This effort has extended to the African", "start": 475.6, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "continent which suffers from the", "start": 478.44, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "devastating effects of climate change.", "start": 480.52, "duration": 7.72}, {"text": "The royal initiative to establish three", "start": 484.92, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "African climate commissions", "start": 488.24, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "for the Congo Basin", "start": 490.88, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "the Sahel region", "start": 492.68, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "and the African island states", "start": 494.44, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "has generated promising momentum to", "start": 497.36, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "strengthen African climate action and", "start": 499.84, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "coordination among the states of the", "start": 502.68, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "continent in addressing these", "start": 505.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "challenges. However, addressing climate", "start": 506.4, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "change cannot", "start": 509.32, "duration": 4.279}, {"text": "rely on national effort alone. It", "start": 510.96, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "requires the provision of affordable and", "start": 513.599, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "accessible financing technology transfer", "start": 516.88, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "and genuine international solidarity", "start": 520.24, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "enabling developing countries to fulfill", "start": 522.68, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "their responsibilities towards present", "start": 525.48, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "and future generations alike.", "start": 528.2, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Mr. President", "start": 531.44, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "Madam President, the Palestinian", "start": 533.72, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "question remains a constant priority in", "start": 535.72, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "the foreign policy of the Kingdom of", "start": 538.04, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "Morocco based on its belief in the", "start": 539.96, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "justice of this", "start": 542.839, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "that this is a just cause and it's", "start": 545.04, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "central to achieving peace and stability", "start": 547.56, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "in the Middle East region. Building on", "start": 549.44, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "this conviction", "start": 551.72, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "the Kingdom of Morocco under the", "start": 553.44, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "leadership of His Majesty King Mohammed", "start": 555.2, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "the VI", "start": 557.2, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "believes that the establishment of a", "start": 559.24, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "lasting peace in the Middle East depends", "start": 561.0, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "on the establishment of an independent,", "start": 563.16, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "sovereign, and viable Palestinian state", "start": 565.4, "duration": 7.24}, {"text": "on the borders of the 4th of June 1967", "start": 568.839, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "with East Jerusalem as its capital", "start": 572.64, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "living side by side with a state of", "start": 575.64, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "Israel in peace and security.", "start": 578.12, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "In the face of the tragedy that the", "start": 581.36, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "brotherly Palestinian people continue to", "start": 583.24, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "endure, the kingdom renews its call for", "start": 585.44, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "respect for the ceasefire", "start": 588.72, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "in Gaza and for the entry of", "start": 591.28, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "humanitarian assistance into the strip", "start": 592.96, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "in sufficient quantities without", "start": 595.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "impediment or interruption.", "start": 597.44, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "At the same time,", "start": 599.6, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Morocco stresses the need to support the", "start": 601.36, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "Palestinian Authority, particularly in", "start": 603.68, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "the financial, technical, structural,", "start": 605.96, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "humanitarian, and training fields, and", "start": 608.16, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "to accompany the reforms it is", "start": 611.48, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "undertaking within its various", "start": 613.96, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "institutions.", "start": 616.04, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "Morocco also renews its support for the", "start": 617.88, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "pivotal role of the United Nations", "start": 620.24, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "Relief and Works Agency for Palestine", "start": 622.92, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "refugees in the Near East, UNRWA. In", "start": 625.64, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "keeping with its approach of supporting", "start": 628.6, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "initiatives aimed at achieving peace in", "start": 630.64, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "the Middle East,", "start": 632.92, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Morocco has decided to participate in", "start": 634.56, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "the international stabilization force in", "start": 637.0, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "Gaza", "start": 639.16, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "and to contribute through humanitarian", "start": 640.32, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "and security initiatives", "start": 642.76, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "to establishing a climate of peace and", "start": 644.6, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "security in the region", "start": 646.76, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "by contributing to the training of the", "start": 648.48, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "Palestinian police,", "start": 650.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "deploying high-ranking military officers", "start": 652.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "to the internal security forces, and", "start": 655.16, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "setting up a military field hospital in", "start": 657.4, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "addition to its readiness to lead a", "start": 660.32, "duration": 6.36}, {"text": "program to counter extremism.", "start": 662.76, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Developments in the West Bank are deeply", "start": 666.68, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "alarming, including the adoption of", "start": 668.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "certain laws that affect the legal", "start": 670.72, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "status of Palestinian territory and pave", "start": 673.16, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "the way for their seizure for the", "start": 676.48, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "purpose of settlement expansion, as well", "start": 678.52, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "as the systematic violence perpetrated", "start": 680.68, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "by Israeli settlers against Palestinian", "start": 683.44, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "citizens.", "start": 686.36, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "All these measures", "start": 687.56, "duration": 3.96}, {"text": "point in one direction,", "start": 689.56, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "the displacement of the population, and", "start": 691.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the undermining of the material bases", "start": 693.92, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "for the establishment of an independent", "start": 696.4, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Palestinian state. With regard to the", "start": 698.28, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "city of Jerusalem, Morocco expresses its", "start": 700.12, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "deep concern about unilateral Israeli", "start": 702.64, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "measures", "start": 705.04, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "and the repeated violations", "start": 706.4, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "of the sanctity of Al-Aqsa Mosque, which", "start": 709.2, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "constitutes serious transgressions that", "start": 712.12, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "contribute to fueling the discourse of", "start": 715.12, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "extremism and hatred at the expense of", "start": 717.72, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "the voice of wisdom and moderation.", "start": 720.24, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "As the chair of Al-Quds Committee, His", "start": 722.84, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "Majesty King Mohammed VI, may God assist", "start": 725.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "him, continues his work to preserve the", "start": 727.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "historical, cultural, and spiritual", "start": 730.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "identity of the holy city and its legal", "start": 732.16, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "status, as well as to improve the living", "start": 734.92, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "conditions of the Maghdisi inhabitants,", "start": 737.4, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "combining", "start": 740.56, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "political and diplomatic action with", "start": 742.04, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "programs implemented on the ground by", "start": 744.08, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "Bayt Mal Al-Quds Al-Sharif agency, the", "start": 747.12, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "executive arm of Al-Quds Committee.", "start": 750.6, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "Mr. President, despite its significant", "start": 757.96, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "human, natural, and civilizational", "start": 760.0, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "assets, the African continent faces a", "start": 762.2, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "gap between the scale of the commitments", "start": 764.4, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "announced for its benefit by the", "start": 766.92, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "international community and the value of", "start": 768.96, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "what has actually been achieved on the", "start": 770.72, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "ground. Contrary to the stereotypical", "start": 772.32, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "image held by some, Africa is not a", "start": 774.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "continent of conflicts and a hotbed of", "start": 777.4, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "problems. Rather, it is a land of", "start": 779.72, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "opportunity and potential, capable of", "start": 781.92, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "devising solutions and putting forward", "start": 785.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "initiatives.", "start": 787.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "That is the idea summed up by His", "start": 789.72, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "Majesty King Mohammed VI, may God assist", "start": 791.6, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "him, in his eloquent words, \"Africa must", "start": 794.4, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "trust Africa.\" End of quote. The", "start": 797.4, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "enlightened royal vision for Africa,", "start": 799.32, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "which has materialized through a", "start": 801.76, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "significant number of projects,", "start": 803.64, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "stems from a firm conviction that the", "start": 806.52, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "continent has attained a level of", "start": 809.04, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "maturity that qualifies it to", "start": 811.08, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "participate effectively in all decisions", "start": 813.2, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "relating to its affairs.", "start": 816.12, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "Indeed, it is capable of contributing to", "start": 818.84, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "formulating proposals and solutions to", "start": 821.12, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "the challenges facing the world as a", "start": 823.96, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "whole.", "start": 825.8, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "Morocco has translated this vision into", "start": 827.64, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "practical and tangible royal", "start": 829.8, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "initiatives.", "start": 831.36, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "The most prominent of which are perhaps", "start": 833.4, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "the royal initiative to enable Sahel", "start": 835.88, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "states to access the Atlantic Ocean,", "start": 838.04, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "as well as the African Atlantic states", "start": 842.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "process,", "start": 844.84, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the African Atlantic gas pipeline", "start": 846.8, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "project, as well as investments in", "start": 849.72, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "regional infrastructure, cooperation in", "start": 851.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the areas of food security, fertilizer", "start": 853.76, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "production, and training programs for", "start": 856.4, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "African executives. This is in addition", "start": 858.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "to partnerships in the areas of health,", "start": 860.84, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "renewable energy, and water resource", "start": 863.36, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "management.", "start": 865.52, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "Madam President,", "start": 867.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "with regard to the North African region,", "start": 869.08, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "thanks to the momentum initiated by His", "start": 873.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Majesty King Mohammed VI, may God assist", "start": 875.32, "duration": 7.88}, {"text": "him, the question of the Moroccan Sahara", "start": 878.36, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "reached a historic turning point with", "start": 883.2, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "the adoption by the Security Council of", "start": 885.72, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "resolution 2797", "start": 887.839, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "last October.", "start": 890.32, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "Since then,", "start": 892.16, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "this regional dispute", "start": 894.36, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "has embarked on an irreversible course,", "start": 897.0, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "breaking with the past and looking to", "start": 900.24, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "the future", "start": 902.4, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "with a view to its final settlement.", "start": 903.96, "duration": 8.52}, {"text": "This track rests on principles and", "start": 908.12, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "parameters that admit no interpretation", "start": 912.48, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "nor any reading between the lines", "start": 915.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "or in the margins, as some are vainly", "start": 918.44, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "attempting,", "start": 921.16, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "deluding themselves in flagrant denial", "start": 922.68, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "of reality and total disregard for", "start": 924.96, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "established truth.", "start": 927.76, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "These principles,", "start": 929.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "as set forth in this critical", "start": 931.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "resolution, are as follows. First,", "start": 933.36, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "there is no solution outside the", "start": 936.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "framework of the autonomy under Moroccan", "start": 937.96, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "sovereignty. Second, there is no", "start": 941.36, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "approach or mechanism other than the", "start": 943.4, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "political negotiation process under the", "start": 945.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "auspices of the United Nations and on a", "start": 948.4, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "sole basis, namely the autonomy", "start": 951.24, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "initiative", "start": 953.2, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "presented by the Kingdom of Morocco.", "start": 955.04, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Third,", "start": 957.08, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "there can be no discussion or dispute", "start": 958.76, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "regarding the responsibility and", "start": 961.0, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "obligations of the four parties clearly", "start": 962.68, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "identified by Security Council", "start": 965.28, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "resolution 2797.", "start": 967.64, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "Fourth, there will be no maintaining of", "start": 970.64, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "the status quo preferred by the other", "start": 972.88, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "parties.", "start": 974.76, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "The train of political solution has", "start": 977.32, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "already departed.", "start": 979.32, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Fifth, there is no credibility for", "start": 981.0, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "interlocutors who violate the ceasefire", "start": 983.24, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "and refuse to respect Security Council", "start": 986.72, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "resolutions. Sixth and last, there can", "start": 988.56, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "be no tolerance for the continued", "start": 991.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "holding of the population of the camps", "start": 993.04, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "as hostages for a half a century in", "start": 995.8, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "flagrant violation of international law", "start": 999.16, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "and international humanitarian law.", "start": 1001.72, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "Alongside with its firm commitment to", "start": 1004.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the final settlement of this regional", "start": 1006.48, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "dispute,", "start": 1009.28, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "affected regional dispute, the Kingdom", "start": 1010.88, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "of Morocco steadfastly continues to", "start": 1013.36, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "drive social and economic development in", "start": 1015.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "its southern provinces, particularly in", "start": 1017.76, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "areas of infrastructure, university", "start": 1020.76, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "education,", "start": 1023.08, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "health sector, and airports, among", "start": 1024.48, "duration": 3.16}, {"text": "others.", "start": 1026.56, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "It is a fortunate coincidence", "start": 1027.64, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "that", "start": 1030.319, "duration": 2.561}, {"text": "tomorrow, God willing, the inhabitants", "start": 1033.079, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "of these Saharan provinces will fulfill", "start": 1035.88, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "their national and political duty by", "start": 1038.199, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "participating as they have always done", "start": 1040.88, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "in the past in the legislative elections", "start": 1042.839, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "of the kingdom. In so doing, they will", "start": 1045.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "strengthen democratic representation and", "start": 1047.4, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "contribute to the day-to-day management", "start": 1049.88, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "of the needs of the inhabitants of the", "start": 1052.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Moroccan provinces. Madam President, the", "start": 1054.64, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Kingdom of Morocco, true to its constant", "start": 1057.6, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "approach, is determined to contribute", "start": 1060.24, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "effectively and responsibly to the", "start": 1062.92, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "maintenance of international peace and", "start": 1065.32, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "security.", "start": 1067.04, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "This is done in accordance with a", "start": 1068.44, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "realistic vision of international", "start": 1070.88, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "cooperation grounded in solidarity and", "start": 1072.84, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "with full respect for international law,", "start": 1075.64, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "national sovereignty, and territorial", "start": 1077.96, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "integrity.", "start": 1079.56, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "It is in this context that the Kingdom", "start": 1081.4, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "of Morocco has presented its candidacy", "start": 1083.48, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "for a non-permanent seat on the Security", "start": 1086.24, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "Council for the term 2028-2029,", "start": 1088.96, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "so that it may continue to serve peace,", "start": 1092.68, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "collective security,", "start": 1096.08, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "and multilateralism", "start": 1098.16, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "with full respect for the purposes and", "start": 1100.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "principles enshrined in the Charter of", "start": 1102.68, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "the United Nations.", "start": 1105.44, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "It is the candidacy of a kingdom with a", "start": 1108.0, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "diplomatic heritage spanning several", "start": 1111.24, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "centuries, which carries the vision of", "start": 1113.52, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "His Majesty King Mohammed VI, may God", "start": 1115.68, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "assist him, as an actor for stability,", "start": 1118.52, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "as an anchor for stability,", "start": 1121.6, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "and sustainable development in the", "start": 1123.8, "duration": 2.72}, {"text": "world.", "start": 1125.44, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "This candidacy also reflects the", "start": 1126.52, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "continued contribution of the Kingdom of", "start": 1129.16, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Morocco to the three pillars of the", "start": 1131.28, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "United Nations, namely peace,", "start": 1133.96, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "development, and the rule of law. I", "start": 1136.52, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "thank you.", "start": 1138.4, "duration": 2.6}, {"text": ">> I thank the Minister of Foreign Affairs,", "start": 1148.0, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "African Cooperation, and Moroccans", "start": 1150.96, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "Abroad of Morocco.", "start": 1153.08, "duration": 3.44}]